<title>USA: Clothing top air cargo import into New York.</title>
<headline>Clothing top air cargo import into New York.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Clothing imports totalling 110,304 tonnes were made through cargo hubs located at John F. Kennedy and Newark airports between January - September 1996, the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey said.</p>
<p>The combined tonnage for the two cargo hubs of the top ten imported commodities were:</p>
<p>						Jan-Sept 96   Jan-Sept 95</p>
<p> 1  Apparel				 110,304	 113,437</p>
<p> 2  Computer Parts			 34,302	  33,311</p>
<p> 3  Edible Vegetables		    26,544	  22.301</p>
<p> 4  Electronics/Machinery		22,544	  24,700</p>
<p> 5  Foot Wear				15,278	  20,555</p>
<p> 6  Optical/Photographic Equipment   14,806	  14,533</p>
<p> 7  Printed Books			  13,345	  13,187</p>
<p> 8  Fish/Crustacean			10,819	   9,903</p>
<p> 9  Leather				   9,735	  10,026</p>
<p> 10 Plastics				  9,150	   9,658</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
